          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.592,
            0.11
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does it decrease by the same rate (or factor)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.112,
            0.846,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Going by bicycle is 3 times faster than walking "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 5 \\div 5 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The speed has increased 3 times. The travel time has decreased 3 times too "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( 1 8 \\div 6 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The speed has increased by the same factor by which the travel time has decreased."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.189,
            0.701,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Check if this is the case for the other modes of transport."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.214,
            0.845,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since both quantities, speed and time, change by the same factor, they are proportional. But they change in opposite directions, or inversely. Such proportions are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "inverse proportions",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.27,
            0.845,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From the table, we can see that the product of speed and time are the same for all modes of transport, namely 90 km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.319,
            0.847,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "relation of the type "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x y = k ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where k is a constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.368,
            0.846,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the previous example, if x represents the speed and y represents the time taken, then k is the distance between Lucknow and Kanpur, which remains constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.289,
            0.433,
            0.709,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.289,
                0.433,
                0.709,
                0.631
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.643,
            0.845,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, if quantities x and y are inversely proportional, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are values of x that have corresponding y values "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y _ { 2 ^ { \\circ } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.681,
            0.644,
            0.7
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "x_{1}y_{1}=x_{2}y_{2}=k ( some constant )."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.702,
            0.49,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From these we can see that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\overline { { X } } _ { 1 } } { X _ { _ 2 } } = \\frac { \\overline { { y } } _ { 2 } } { \\overline { { y } } _ { 1 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.736,
            0.845,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us check if this is true for other modes of transport, such as walking and by car. Let us use x to represent speed and y to represent time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.357,
            0.773,
            0.639,
            0.795
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "x_{1}=5,x_{2}=60,y_{1}=18,y_{2}=1.5."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.795,
            0.595,
            0.829
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { \\frac { X _ { _ 1 } } { X _ { _ 2 } } = \\frac { 5 } { 6 0 } = 0 . 0 8 3 3 3 3 . . . } \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.833,
            0.623,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the value of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 . 5 } { 1 8 }   \\bigg ( \\cfrac { y _ { 2 } ^ { } } { y _ { 1 } ^ { } } \\bigg ) ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " It is 0.083333... too!"
            }
          ]
        },
